            <ArticleTitle>Postmortem study of the prevalence of gallstones in Athens.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>304-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prevalence of gallstones in Athens in 1973 was studied in an autopsy survey that covered 1,448 subjects of all ages and both sexes. Gallstones were found in 5.2% of all subjects and in 6.2% of subjects older than 40 years. The prevalence was higher in females and considerably higher in persons who died from cirrhosis of the liver or from ischaemic heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
